task: intent-taxon-wired-to-tiers
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-taxon-wired-to-tiers
worktree: ../okay-wt-wired2

why: the last of the three frictions the first caller exposed, parked
  twice for the operator's asks. Request 1 wanted one taxonomy both
  tiers read; what landed is one taxonomy NEITHER trained tier reads.
  Every `train` infers its classes from whatever labels its rows
  happened to carry, and a caller checks agreement by hand afterwards.
  `Router.of` now checks it at the door, which is the composition, not
  the fit.

  The latent bug that makes it more than tidiness: `NoModel.blend`
  adds a cue's weight to a probe class by STRING EQUALITY. If the cues
  speak `Proposal` and the probe was fitted on `MeetingProposal`, the
  bonus never applies and the ensemble silently degrades to the plain
  probe. Nothing today can notice.

what: every `Trained` carries the `Taxon` it was fitted against —
  inferred by `train`, DECLARED by `against(taxon, rows)` which checks
  the labels. `silent` names the classes a tier can never produce.
  `NoModel.fit` refuses cues and a probe that disagree.

files: okay-intent/src/main/scala/okay/intent/{Centroid,Probe,Nearest,
  CharGrams,NoModel}.scala, tests, specs/intent-classify.md, BACKLOG.md
